[114.168226, "o", "--- PAGE 0 --- \r\n Pricing Migration Rule Document\r\nSaaS 2026 Plan Migration — Authoritative Reference\r\nThis document defines all rules governing the migration of SaaS customer accounts from legacy plans\r\nto new 2026 pricing packages. All audit tools must use this document as the sole source of truth for\r\n"]
[114.16848, "o", "plan mapping, price floors, exception handling, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King, rule precedence, and output schemas.\r\n1. Migration Effective Date\r\nParameter Value\r\nMigration effective date 2026-04-01\r\n2. Usage Tier Calculation\r\nUsage tier is determined from trailing 90-day API call volume ending before the migration effective date.\r\n\u001b[36m\u001b[K--\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n7. Expected Monthly Price Calculation\r\nFor each account, the expected monthly price is the greater of two amounts: the plan's published base\r\nmonthly rate (Section 5) and the account's total seat-count obligation — current seats multiplied by the\r\nper-seat floor for the applicable plan (Section 6).\r\nRound monetary values to 2 decimal places.\r\n8. \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KGrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King Rules\r\nSome accounts have a \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[Ked_until date and a price_floor_discount_pct in their contract terms.\r\n\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KGrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King applies to the per-seat price floor only, not the base monthly rate or plan mapping.\r\nWhen \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[Ked_until is on or after migration_effective_date, apply price_floor_discount_pct to the\r\nper-seat floor before computing the seat-count obligation. Normalize contract field encodings before\r\nuse.\r\nIf \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[Ked_until is null or before migration_effective_date, \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King does not apply.\r\n--- PAGE 2 --- \r\n 9. Exception Approval Rules\r\nException approvals are stored in exception_approvals.xlsx.\r\nAn approval is valid when approval_status is approved (after normalizing case and surrounding\r\nwhitespace), effective_date is on or before migration_effective_date, and expiry_date is on or after\r\nmigration_effective_date.\r\nA valid plan_override replaces the mapped plan. A valid price_override replaces the computed monthly\r\nprice.\r\n10. Rule Precedence\r\nDetermine usage tier, then plan mapping, then apply valid plan overrides, then compute price from seat\r\nfloors and \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King, then apply valid price overrides.\r\n11. Violation Types\r\nEach account is assigned exactly one violation_type:\r\nParameter Value\r\nno_violation Expected plan and price match assignment.\r\nusage_tier_miscalculated Assigned plan matches wrong usage tier.\r\nwrong_plan Assigned plan does not match expected plan, not due to usage tier.\r\nwrong_price_floor Plan is correct, but assigned monthly price does not match expected monthly price, and the mismatch is not better explained by an expired exception or missing \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King.\r\nmissing_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King Plan is correct, but assigned price does not reflect the \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King-adjusted seat floor used to compute the expected monthly price.\r\nexpired_exception Assignment relied on an approval whose expiry_date is before migration_effective_date.\r\n12. Required Output Schemas\r\n"]
[114.168757, "o", "migration_audit.csv — one row per account:\r\naccount_id | legacy_plan | usage_tier | expected_new_plan | assigned_new_plan |\r\nexpected_monthly_price | assigned_monthly_price | migration_status | violation_type\r\n| revenue_impact_usd\r\nmigration_status allowed values: pass, fail\r\nviolation_type allowed values: no_violation, usage_tier_miscalculated, wrong_plan, wrong_price_floor,\r\nmissing_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King, expired_exception\r\nrevenue_impact_usd = assigned_monthly_price - expected_monthly_price (positive = overcharged,\r\nnegative = undercharged, zero = pass)\r\nrule_violations.json — summary object with keys:\r\ntotal_accounts, failed_accounts, passed_accounts, violation_counts (dict with keys:\r\nwrong_plan, wrong_price_floor, expired_exception, missing_\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kgrandfather\u001b[m\u001b[King,\r\nusage_tier_miscalculated), highest_revenue_impact_account, net_revenue_impact_usd,\r\n--- PAGE 3 --- \r\n policy_sources\r\npolicy_sources must list: migration_rules.pdf, legacy_accounts.csv, product_usage_events.csv,\r\ncontract_terms.jsonl, exception_approvals.xlsx, new_plan_assignments.csv\r\n"]
